<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Campaign_SumpNoTarRain.xml - SUMP_TAR_LIVING_SYSTEMS_1 part 2, the campaign half. Owner, typed 2026-10-09:
  "Flowworks supports tar rain but campaign does not. The biome itself does except for the campaign. Correct."
  Ruling 1: "Tar rain is part of mod but not this scenario."

  RM_TheSump (mandrake.rm.thesump) ships RM_SumpTarRainLock: permanent dusk with tar-rain spells. In the campaign
  this layer puts the biome back on RUT_SumpDuskLock (dusk, no rain at all), the lock RUT_Sump already carries, so
  the campaign's "no rain" guarantee holds on both Sump defs, including after the planet's final repaint onto RM_
  biomes. Gate: FindMod on the composed biomes mod (RimMandrake.Biomes, which ships TheSump), where the target lives.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>RimMandrake: Baroque Biomes</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_TheSump"]/biomeMapConditions/li[text()="RM_SumpTarRainLock"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>RUT_SumpDuskLock</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
